{
  "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
  "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:06 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Financial Oversight and Management Board for Puerto Rico",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question in this case is whether members of the Financial Oversight Board are officers of the United States who must be selected in the manner that the Appointments Clause prescribes or whether they are instead territorial officers who do not have to be selected in that manner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So how --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mister --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What do we do about the brief --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Verrilli",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that shows the perils of relying on an amicus brief that relies on extra-record information. The vast majority of those -- of the -- the documents there have not been disclosed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We know that Congress expressly invoked its authority over the territories and placed the Board within the Puerto Rican government. So the real question here is, was that choice constitutional under Article IV? It was."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Wouldn't -- wouldn't the officer still be a valid territorial officer but perhaps exercising some duties that he or she cannot exercise?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Olson, I think the basic question, if I can simplify it, I believe, is couldn't the governor of Puerto Rico and the legislature have created their own fiscal rescue plan? Yes. Correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. OLSON: Well, the -- the -- they -- the President appointed one without advice and consent of the Senate. That violates the Appointments Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Congress enacts the\nD.C. code, right? The D.C. code is enacted by\nCongress?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. OLSON: The test -- my test is\nthis Court's test, which was articulated in the\nBuckley case, again in the -- in the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: -- what struck me when\nI read that, when I read your brief, the Buckley\ntest is significant authority pursuant to the\nlaws of the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Mendez-Colberg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They -- the oversight board has the authority, and as Mr. Olson mentioned, has the authority to file this bankruptcy proceedings, which is a federal power, on behalf of the government."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought the argument was that the Appointments Clause does apply to Puerto Rico, and the question is simply whether it's implicated on these particular facts with respect to this particular agency?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "question about the duties of the Board? If the duties of the Board and responsibilities are considered primarily local -- I'll ask the same question I asked Mr. Olson -- do you lose or do you have an alternative argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Which D.C. -- which D.C. judges are you talking about? I thought the judges of the D.C. Superior Court and of the D.C. Court of Appeals are not -- are not federal judges."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Financial Oversight and Management Board for Puerto Rico",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0004-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So that's what will happen if we go down that path. And I would strongly urge the Court not to do that. If you do reach the remedial issue, then I think the de facto officer doctrine, a perfectly reasonable judgment, but more fundamentally, there is no reason to reach the remedial issue --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Financial Oversight and Management Board for Puerto Rico",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0004-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 96,
        "start": 96
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "converted into a federal official because he took Detroit into bankruptcy under Chapter 9. He's still exercising his local power. Same with the Board. And, second, again, the question I think has to be whose interests is -- is the Board advancing in that process? It's the court, the Article III court, that engages in the broad adjustment of interests here to achieve a -- a nationwide result. The Board's job, as the statute expressly says, is to act on behalf of the people of Puerto Rico and the government of Puerto Rico as its representative. It's an advocate for Puerto Rico, and that's why it's territorial authority."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1334",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "95c63a04159cc6945ebe96ea6b415e24b768ffc0129012d9ab9e08f421b7be4d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-95c63a04159c-0004-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 96,
        "start": 96
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
